[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2531647163","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100239#issuecomment-2531647163","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100239","id":2531647163,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6W5d67","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-10T13:31:21Z","updated_at":"2024-12-10T13:31:21Z","body":"I removed the `Variant` move constructor and assignment because MSVC got confused 🫠\r\nMay address that later separately.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2531647163/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2531870983","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100239#issuecomment-2531870983","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100239","id":2531870983,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6W6UkH","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-10T14:53:59Z","updated_at":"2024-12-10T14:53:59Z","body":"> But because of having to use `std::move`, it brings some STL headers, which is against [the Godot Guidelines](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/cpp_usage_guidelines.html), so this needs to be discussed by maintainers\r\n\r\nNotably, `std::move` is already used in the codebase, but _very_ rarely. The usage guidelines more pertain to _using_ STL, I think, rather than simply including it.\r\n\r\n> Maybe you could propose a godot version of move ?\r\n\r\nI guess that would be possible, but is it really that important to avoid include `<utility>`?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2531870983/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2531954879","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100239#issuecomment-2531954879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100239","id":2531954879,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6W6pC_","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-10T15:09:50Z","updated_at":"2024-12-10T15:54:51Z","body":"> > But because of having to use `std::move`, it brings some STL headers, which is against [the Godot Guidelines](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/cpp_usage_guidelines.html), so this needs to be discussed by maintainers\r\n> \r\n> Notably, `std::move` is already used in the codebase, but _very_ rarely. The usage guidelines more pertain to _using_ STL, I think, rather than simply including it.\r\n> \r\n> > Maybe you could propose a godot version of move ?\r\n> \r\n> I guess that would be possible, but is it really that important to avoid include `<utility>`?\r\n\r\nTo be honest I don't know. The only `std::move` in Godot I found that is not in thirdparty is from one of my PR, interacting with third party code in the engine. I would be for it, but adding it here is really more **core**, so I guess you'll need maintainers opinions.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2531954879/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2532331996","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100239#issuecomment-2532331996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100239","id":2532331996,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6W8FHc","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-10T17:17:41Z","updated_at":"2024-12-10T17:17:41Z","body":"We can use things from std::, it is fine. We use std::thread already. The rule only applies to STL containers and such. Using std::move in this context is 100% fine.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2532331996/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2532358194","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100239#issuecomment-2532358194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100239","id":2532358194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6W8Lgy","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-10T17:30:00Z","updated_at":"2024-12-10T17:30:00Z","body":"All looks really straightforwardly correct, I'll run some tests later but I have no style or technical comments.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2532358194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2533378988","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100239#issuecomment-2533378988","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100239","id":2533378988,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XAEus","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-11T01:02:12Z","updated_at":"2024-12-11T01:02:12Z","body":"Just for background. At the contributor meeting this past October we had a long discussion about including certain modern C++ features. We talked about move specifically in detail and the consensus was:\r\n1. Move can be very useful, especially inside core containers\r\n2. But it is a fairly niche feature that most contributors aren't familiar with\r\n3. Therefore, we shouldnt use it wisely across the engine, but should implement it in certain core containers where we can get the most benefit. \r\n\r\nI think this PR is in line with our discussion. HP and I also discussed a few other places in core that would benefit from using move. \r\n\r\nThat being said, we need to be careful about where we use it an how. We shouldn't just be adding move wherever we see a place that it can fit, we should check everything with a profiler and ensure we are actually having an impact and not needlessly making our code difficult to read","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2533378988/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540144296","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100239#issuecomment-2540144296","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100239","id":2540144296,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XZ4ao","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T22:34:01Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T22:34:01Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2540144296/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]